<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n148" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbŏlĭtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an
				abrogating</i>, <i>annulling</i>, <i>abolishing</i>, <i>abolition</i> (postAug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tributorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 13, 50</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadragesimae quinquagesimaeque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sententiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					6, 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>An amnesty</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Tib. 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 4, 7, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub pacto abolitionis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 2, 97</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In the
			Dig., <i>the withdrawal of an accusation</i> or <i>suit</i>, <i>suspension</i>: abolitio
			publica, ex lege, privata, Cod. Th. 9, 37, 3 sq.; <i><span class="en">Dig. 48,
				16 al.</span></i>; cf. Rein, Criminalrecht. p. 273 sq.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
